{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["And as for what is written 'לַאֲלָפִים,' while at the end of parashat Va'etḥannan it is written (Deuteronomy 7:9) 'שֹׁמֵר הַבְּרִית וְהַחֶסֶד לְאֹהֲבָיו וּלְשֹׁמְרֵי מִצְוֹתָיו לְאֶלֶף דּוֹר' — it appears to me that it is all one reckoning. For the measure of goodness is twice twofold, alluded to in the בְּרִית and the חֶסֶד, which is 'לְאֶלֶךְ דּוֹר' — that is, the keeping of חֶסֶד alone without בְּרִית is לַאֲלָפִים. And in the Gemara (Sotah 31a) they resolved it: one is from love, one is from fear."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:21:40.015323722Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}